# Dark Factory — instance configuration
#
# Copy this file to deploy/instance.env (gitignored) and fill in your values.
# Always start compose with --env-file so FACTORY_INSTANCE, PROJECT_DIR and IMAGE_TAG/IMAGE_REF
# below also reach compose interpolation:
#
#   docker compose --env-file deploy/instance.env -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d
#
# This file configures the SCHEDULER. Dispatched run containers do not read it: they
# get their secrets from <PROJECT_DIR>/.archon/.env (see docs/onboarding-new-target.md).
#
# The identity block is printed ready-to-paste by:
#   scripts/bootstrap_target.sh OWNER/REPO
# Leaving identity vars blank or unset makes the image fall back to MarketHawk's
# values, which WILL NOT work for any other repo or board.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication (required — no defaults)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GitHub token with repo + project + workflow scope (e.g. `gh auth token`).
GH_TOKEN=

# Claude authentication: CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (subscription; create one with
# `claude setup-token`) or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (direct API billing).
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compose / host wiring
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Scopes container names and the scheduler state volume; one value per target so
# several instances can share a host. Convention: the repo name. Must be a normalized
# compose project name ([a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*); see the build-network block below.
FACTORY_INSTANCE=

# Absolute host path of your target repo checkout (mounted read-only at
# /workspace/project). The scheduler reads <PROJECT_DIR>/.archon/.env from it and,
# optionally, <PROJECT_DIR>/config/config.yaml. Runs always clone fresh from GitHub.
# Windows: use forward slashes, e.g. C:/git/my-repo
PROJECT_DIR=

# Optional: pin the factory image (default: ghcr.io/omniscient/dark-factory:latest).
# IMAGE_TAG selects a tag; IMAGE_REF overrides the whole reference and is the way to
# pin a digest. Recommended when several instances share a host, since they
# otherwise share the local :latest. Get the current digest with:
#   docker image inspect ghcr.io/omniscient/dark-factory:latest --format '{{index .RepoDigests 0}}'
# IMAGE_TAG=latest
# IMAGE_REF=ghcr.io/omniscient/dark-factory@sha256:<digest>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instance identity (REQUIRED — paste the block from scripts/bootstrap_target.sh)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# GitHub owner and repo of the target (the repo whose issues the factory works).
FACTORY_OWNER=
FACTORY_REPO=

# Projects v2 board: node ID (PVT_…) and the number shown in the board URL.
FACTORY_PROJECT_ID=
FACTORY_PROJECT_NUMBER=

# Status field node ID (PVTSSF_…) and the option ID of each of the 7 columns.
FACTORY_STATUS_FIELD=
FACTORY_STATUS_READY=
FACTORY_STATUS_IN_PROGRESS=
FACTORY_STATUS_IN_REVIEW=
FACTORY_STATUS_BLOCKED=
FACTORY_STATUS_DONE=
FACTORY_STATUS_BACKLOG=
FACTORY_STATUS_REFINED=

# Human-readable product name used in issue comments and log markers.
FACTORY_PRODUCT_NAME=

# Path inside the run container where entrypoint.sh clones the target, and the
# prefix for run container names. Convention: /workspace/<repo>, <repo>-dark-factory-run-
FACTORY_CLONE_DIR=
FACTORY_RUN_PREFIX=

# Manual lookups, if you are not using the bootstrap script:
#   gh project view <NUMBER> --owner <OWNER> --format json --jq .id
#   gh project field-list <NUMBER> --owner <OWNER> --format json \
#     --jq '.fields[] | select(.name=="Status") | {id, options}'
# (MarketHawk's own values live in deploy/instances/markethawk/instance.env.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduler tuning (optional — defaults are safe for most deployments)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Max concurrent factory containers (default: 1).
FACTORY_WIP_LIMIT=1

# Seconds between board polls (default: 60).
POLL_INTERVAL=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider selection (optional — defaults are github / github / anthropic, see #489)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set here, these reach the scheduler AND every dispatched run container: scheduler.sh
# forwards each one that is set and non-empty as `docker compose run -e NAME`
# (scripts/provider_env.sh holds the full list). Unset or empty = nothing is forwarded and
# .archon/.env stays in control; a non-empty value here WINS over the same name in
# .archon/.env. Leave all of these unset for a default GitHub/Anthropic deployment.
#
# FACTORY_TRACKER=github          # github | jira
# FACTORY_CODEHOST=github         # github (gitlab is a seam proof, not selectable yet)
# FACTORY_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic  # anthropic | bedrock | vertex (databricks/openai not implemented)
#
# Tracker jira (required when FACTORY_TRACKER=jira):
# JIRA_BASE_URL=
# JIRA_PROJECT_KEY=
# JIRA_TOKEN=                     # secret; forwarded like the rest
# JIRA_EPIC_LINK_FIELD=
# Optional: JIRA_ISSUE_TYPE=Task, JIRA_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=30
#
# Code host gitlab (seam proof): GITLAB_TOKEN= (secret), optional GITLAB_BASE_URL=gitlab.com
#
# Model provider bedrock: CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK=1, AWS_REGION=, and AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID /
#   AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY (or AWS_PROFILE / AWS_ROLE_ARN / AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE /
#   AWS_SESSION_TOKEN)
# Model provider vertex: CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX=1, ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=, CLOUD_ML_REGION=,
#   and GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS= (or GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT with ADC)
#
# Which file? The scheduler's boot preflight reads only THIS file's environment, so every
# provider variable the selected providers need must be here. The variables above are also
# forwarded to run containers, so they need not be duplicated in <PROJECT_DIR>/.archon/.env
# (a copy there is harmless; a non-empty value here overrides it). Exception: GH_TOKEN,
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY are deliberately NOT forwarded; run containers
# take those from .archon/.env only, exactly as before.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transparent model traffic proxy (optional — default off, see #208)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Opt in to routing Claude Code traffic through factory-model-proxy for a
# per-request ledger (docs/dark-factory-model-proxy-rollout.md). Default
# unset/false = today's direct-to-Anthropic behavior, byte-for-byte.
# FACTORY_MODEL_PROXY_ENABLED=true

# Required alongside FACTORY_MODEL_PROXY_ENABLED, but NOT in this file: set
#   ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://factory-model-proxy:8787
# in <PROJECT_DIR>/.archon/.env, the env_file of run containers. This file only
# reaches the scheduler, and the scheduler does not forward ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL,
# so setting it here starts the proxy with no traffic through it. See
# docs/dark-factory-model-proxy-rollout.md.

# Opt-in raw request/response artifact capture (off by default — the compact
# ledger has no payload content; raw artifacts do, including system prompts
# and code diffs). Retention: RAW_ARTIFACT_RETENTION_DAYS (default 7).
# RAW_ARTIFACT_CAPTURE=true
# RAW_ARTIFACT_RETENTION_DAYS=7

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Target build daemon / preview network (optional — most targets skip this, #455)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Only for targets whose preview builds run on their own remote BuildKit daemon
# (the built-in preview-up path builds via tcp://$BUILDKIT_HOST:$BUILDKIT_PORT).
# Leave all three unset otherwise. They are then a no-op: run containers join no
# extra network and BuildKit falls back to buildkit:1234, as before.
#
# FACTORY_BUILD_NETWORK: an existing external Docker network carrying the daemon; run
# containers join it alongside their own dark-factory-net. The network must exist
# before the scheduler dispatches; check with
#   docker network inspect $FACTORY_BUILD_NETWORK
# Once set, it is a hard dependency of EVERY dispatch of this instance, not only
# preview tickets. While it is missing, each dispatch fails with the socket proxy's
# "403 Forbidden ... Request forbidden by administrative rules" (compose's fallback
# lookup hits /info, which the proxy denies), a dispatch_error, and repeated failures
# trip the breaker and move tickets to Blocked. That 403 means "create/restore the
# network", not "widen the proxy". If the network exists but BuildKit is down (or the
# BUILDKIT_* values are wrong), only preview tickets fail, with a generic preview_fail
# "buildx build ... failed" comment that names neither the network nor the address.
#
# When FACTORY_BUILD_NETWORK is unset, the default is <FACTORY_INSTANCE>_dark-factory-net,
# so FACTORY_INSTANCE must already be a normalized compose project name
# ([a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*); otherwise the build-network default points at a network that
# does not exist and every dispatch fails.
#
# BUILDKIT_HOST / BUILDKIT_PORT: the daemon's name (container name or alias) on that
# network and its port. Example (MarketHawk):
# FACTORY_BUILD_NETWORK=markethawk_factory-network
# BUILDKIT_HOST=markethawk-buildkit
# BUILDKIT_PORT=1234
